WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:07.766
Meet VoxTexto, a project by Leandro Augusto Ferreira that
turns audio and video into text documents.

2
00:00:08.016 --> 00:00:15.864
The application brings speech recognition, a file queue and
history together in a web interface with local processing.

3
00:00:17.225 --> 00:00:26.945
Version 1.2.1 adds OGG support alongside MP3, WAV, MP4 and
M4A.

4
00:00:27.195 --> 00:00:34.827
Select files or a folder, or drag media into the panel. The
selection button and compact format badges are centered.

5
00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:43.455
In the queue, each file has its own status and processing
time. Whisper runs in a separate process.

6
00:00:43.705 --> 00:00:51.505
You can pause between files or cancel processing. A
dedicated panel helps you follow the task sequence.

7
00:00:52.892 --> 00:01:00.956
This sample OGG audio was actually transcribed. The result
appears in the interface once speech recognition is
complete.

8
00:01:01.206 --> 00:01:10.398
A Word document is generated automatically and can be
downloaded for review. Processing time depends on the
computer and the file.

9
00:01:11.767 --> 00:01:19.303
History keeps records linked to each account, with the file
name, status, size and processing time.

10
00:01:19.553 --> 00:01:27.065
Search for a transcription, filter results and reopen the
text or Word document without running recognition again.

11
00:01:28.433 --> 00:01:37.145
Dark, Light and HUD themes let you adjust the visual
experience. Interface preferences are saved for each user.

12
00:01:37.395 --> 00:01:44.091
The application also includes sign-in, hashed passwords, and
user and administrator roles.

13
00:01:45.475 --> 00:01:52.987
Statistics summarize account results, including status
distribution, volume and processing time.

14
00:01:53.237 --> 00:02:00.101
OGG also appears in this view alongside the other supported
formats.

15
00:02:01.475 --> 00:02:10.283
VoxTexto combines Python, Flask, Whisper, FFmpeg and SQLite
to connect media selection with document generation.

16
00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:19.797
Explore the screens and source code in the portfolio. The
OGG update is demonstrated here, and the new Windows
installer is the next step.
